WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.878
Vinnie and Mandy could not believe their eyes.

2
00:00:03.879 --> 00:00:07.131
They followed Charlotte through the factory.

3
00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:14.511
Every room was filled with factory workers: men, women, and children.

4
00:00:14.512 --> 00:00:20.900
"Florence, why are children working in the factory?" asked Mandy.

5
00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:24.011
Florence’s face was serious.

6
00:00:24.012 --> 00:00:27.980
"For their families, Miss Mandy," she said.

7
00:00:27.981 --> 00:00:34.025
"People want British products, so our factories must stay busy.

8
00:00:34.026 --> 00:00:38.907
That means everyone, including poor children, must work."

9
00:00:38.908 --> 00:00:44.318
It didn’t seem fair to Mandy, but she kept quiet.

10
00:00:44.319 --> 00:00:48.281
Loud noises came from a nearby room.

11
00:00:48.282 --> 00:00:55.289
They went in and saw huge machines with big metal rollers moving back and forth.

12
00:00:55.290 --> 00:01:00.636
"They look like mechanical weaving machines!"

13
00:01:00.637 --> 00:01:04.585
Mandy cried, but no one heard her.

14
00:01:04.586 --> 00:01:10.014
The sound was so loud that she had to put her fingers in her ears.

15
00:01:10.015 --> 00:01:15.652
"Miss Charlotte!" yelled a man carrying a stack of paper under one arm.

16
00:01:15.653 --> 00:01:20.208
"Mr. Geoffrey! I want to see my father,"

17
00:01:20.209 --> 00:01:23.081
Charlotte yelled over the noise.

18
00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:27.097
The man turned and led them out of the noisy room.

19
00:01:27.098 --> 00:01:32.349
"He is very busy, Miss Charlotte," said Mr. Geoffrey.

20
00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:34.603
"He can’t see you now."

21
00:01:34.604 --> 00:01:37.484
Charlotte looked very sad.

22
00:01:37.485 --> 00:01:41.382
"I want him to meet Vinnie and Mandy."

23
00:01:41.383 --> 00:01:44.445
Mr. Geoffrey shook his head.

24
00:01:44.446 --> 00:01:48.290
"Please," pleaded Charlotte.

25
00:01:48.291 --> 00:01:52.280
"I’m sorry, no," said Mr. Geoffrey.

26
00:01:52.281 --> 00:01:56.126
"What are you making here?" Vinnie asked.

27
00:01:56.127 --> 00:01:58.837
"This is a textile factory.

28
00:01:58.838 --> 00:02:04.209
We weave cloth and make clothes," replied Mr. Geoffrey.

29
00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:09.796
"Do all the factories here make clothes?" asked Mandy.

30
00:02:09.797 --> 00:02:15.637
"No, across the street, they make parts for the railroad," he said.

31
00:02:15.638 --> 00:02:19.418
"Why are there so many factories?"

32
00:02:19.419 --> 00:02:22.107
Mandy wanted to know.

33
00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:26.929
Mr. Geoffrey laughed. "The world is changing.

34
00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:29.415
Industry is the future!

35
00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:32.767
If you need something, England can make it."

36
00:02:32.768 --> 00:02:39.203
Since Charlotte was not allowed to see her father, she wanted to leave.

37
00:02:39.204 --> 00:02:44.575
So they left the factory and found the cab driver waiting.

38
00:02:44.576 --> 00:02:48.058
Suddenly, church bells rang.

39
00:02:48.059 --> 00:02:52.378
Vinnie turned to see a large bell tower in the distance.

40
00:02:52.379 --> 00:03:02.497
"That is St. Katherine’s, an old church that escaped the Great Fire in 1666," Florence said proudly.

41
00:03:02.498 --> 00:03:10.250
"The fire destroyed over 87 churches in London, but not St. Katherine’s!"

42
00:03:10.251 --> 00:03:15.847
"Let’s go. It’s teatime!" demanded Charlotte.

43
00:03:15.848 --> 00:03:18.749
She turned to Vinnie and Mandy.

44
00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:22.207
"Would you like to come to my home for tea?"

45
00:03:22.208 --> 00:03:26.399
"We’d love to," they replied.

46
00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.212
They got into the carriage and rode toward Charlotte’s house.

47
00:03:31.213 --> 00:03:36.823
As they passed through the streets, the city changed again.

48
00:03:36.824 --> 00:03:42.222
"How clean and pretty the streets are," Mandy thought.

49
00:03:42.223 --> 00:03:46.192
The houses here were bigger and nicer too.

50
00:03:46.193 --> 00:03:50.804
Charlotte’s house was on a square with several other homes.

51
00:03:50.805 --> 00:03:54.480
A pretty garden was in the middle of the square.

52
00:03:54.481 --> 00:03:57.954
Little children were playing outside.

53
00:03:57.955 --> 00:04:07.236
"What a difference from the other side of London," Mandy said to herself.

